WEBVTT

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:05.561
In this video, you will see what happens when you create a contest in the SoCal Lights app.

00:00:05.561 --> 00:00:10.386
Contest passes are bought on our website, in your browser, not inside the app.

00:00:10.386 --> 00:00:11.394
We start on the map.

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:14.571
Open the SoCal Lights app on your phone.

00:00:17.368 --> 00:00:19.918
On the home page, tap Use my location.

00:00:21.761 --> 00:00:22.741
Then tap Allow.

00:00:24.614 --> 00:00:26.707
The map zooms to where you are.

00:00:26.707 --> 00:00:30.633
There are no events on your street, so tap Show all of Southern California.

00:00:32.327 --> 00:00:37.119
Now every place shows how far away it is, nearest first, so you can plan your drive.

00:00:38.644 --> 00:00:41.851
Now look at the top of the map, beside the search box.

00:00:41.851 --> 00:00:44.634
See your picture, or your initial, in a circle?

00:00:44.634 --> 00:00:49.197
That is your account menu, and it is the doorway to everything else on the site.

00:00:49.197 --> 00:00:49.898
Tap it.

00:00:52.503 --> 00:00:55.502
In the menu, tap Add an event, home or contest.

00:00:57.098 --> 00:01:01.850
That is where you add anything new: an event, a contest, or your own home.

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:03.491
This is the Add page.

00:01:03.491 --> 00:01:05.100
It has three choices.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:08.695
An event, like a tree lighting or a holiday parade.

00:01:08.695 --> 00:01:13.591
A contest, where neighbors enter their homes, and the community votes for a favorite.

00:01:13.591 --> 00:01:16.278
Or a lighting display, to show off your own home.

00:01:17.068 --> 00:01:19.734
We are creating a contest, so tap A contest.

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:22.688
First, the name.

00:01:22.688 --> 00:01:28.905
This is the title everyone sees, on the contest page, on the map, and in the emails your neighbors get.

00:01:28.905 --> 00:01:34.409
Something simple and local works best, like your street or neighborhood, and the year.

00:01:34.409 --> 00:01:37.828
I will type Oak Hill Holiday Lights 2027.

00:01:37.828 --> 00:01:38.989
Then tap Next.

00:01:40.987 --> 00:01:43.192
Next, who is running it, and where.

00:01:43.192 --> 00:01:44.846
Type the name of your group.

00:01:44.846 --> 00:01:51.161
It can be a city, a school, an H O A, a club, a business, or just your neighbors on one street.

00:01:51.161 --> 00:01:53.194
Then pick the city the homes are in.

00:01:53.194 --> 00:01:56.207
That is how your contest shows up for the right neighbors.

00:01:56.207 --> 00:01:57.044
Tap Next.

00:01:58.749 --> 00:02:00.874
This is the welcome message.

00:02:00.874 --> 00:02:06.907
Neighbors read it before they decide to enter, so it is your chance to say what the contest is about.

00:02:06.907 --> 00:02:08.989
We already wrote a friendly one for you.

00:02:08.989 --> 00:02:12.869
You can keep it as it is, or change a few words so it sounds like you.

00:02:12.869 --> 00:02:13.720
Tap Next.

00:02:15.416 --> 00:02:17.260
A website is optional.

00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:22.464
If your group has one, add it here, and people can see who is behind the contest.

00:02:22.464 --> 00:02:26.569
Your contest goes live right away either way, so it is fine to skip this.

00:02:26.569 --> 00:02:27.408
Tap Next.

00:02:29.134 --> 00:02:29.915
Now the dates.

00:02:29.915 --> 00:02:30.935
There are three.

00:02:30.935 --> 00:02:33.331
The last day neighbors can enter.

00:02:33.331 --> 00:02:34.749
The day voting starts.

00:02:34.749 --> 00:02:36.088
And the day voting ends.

00:02:38.152 --> 00:02:42.199
Entries and voting open and close on these dates by themselves.

00:02:42.199 --> 00:02:45.307
We filled in typical dates, so you can just tap Next.

00:02:46.870 --> 00:02:49.496
You can change any of them later, from your dashboard.

00:02:50.357 --> 00:02:52.345
Choose Quick start, then tap Next.

00:02:54.693 --> 00:02:56.091
This is the review.

00:02:56.091 --> 00:03:00.153
Your organization has no pass yet, so the app tells you how to get one.

00:03:01.867 --> 00:03:04.767
Running a contest needs a contest pass.

00:03:04.767 --> 00:03:09.019
Passes are bought on our website, in your browser, not inside the app.

00:03:09.019 --> 00:03:13.426
The app shows no prices, and it never opens a payment page.

00:03:13.426 --> 00:03:13.788
app.

00:03:13.788 --> 00:03:23.379
It opens the pass page in your browser, with this contest's website, so the pass goes to the same organization.

00:03:23.379 --> 00:03:27.226
Choose a pass there, and pay on Stripe's secure page.

00:03:27.226 --> 00:03:28.867
Then come back to the app.

00:03:28.867 --> 00:03:31.050
Your contest details are kept here.

00:03:31.050 --> 00:03:34.798
Tap I have my pass, and your contest is created.

00:03:34.798 --> 00:03:39.191
If you tap it before you have a pass, the app tells you it does not see one yet.

00:03:39.191 --> 00:03:41.348
Finish on the website, then tap again.

00:03:43.415 --> 00:03:46.092
That is how a contest pass works in the app.

00:03:46.092 --> 00:03:48.506
You choose it on the website, and then come back.

00:03:49.863 --> 00:03:51.693
Next up: Contest passes.
